hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer question  from one of my newsletter readers who  wants to start a coffee shop that  donates a dollar from every coffee sale  to support a local hospital and one of  my advice on how to get started doesn't  have the money to launch the business  and needed some help so to help with  this question I think the first thing  that you need to think about for your  business is you need to get to the  survival point so it's great to be able  to support charity and I'm a big  believer in you know giving back to the  community for us we do a lot of work  with an organization called Kiva that  we've helped raise over fifty thousand  dollars for but the thing is your  business you have to make sure that it's  going to be around for long term so that  you're going to be able to help a lot  more people through your company so you  have to be able to get your company to  you know survival point where you're  able to pay your bills you know live the  lifestyle that you're you know going  after and then make extra money that you  can hopefully you know give back to the  charity so if you're starting a business  that's all around the charity not that  it's a bad idea but you're less likely  to be able to hit the success and have a  big impact that I assume you're try to  have so if you're starting a business  and half the money goes to the charity  for example and you're not able to build  your business to that survival point  then if you closed down in three months  how much of an impact have you had on  that charity where if you were to build  a business and maybe give a little less  at the start still have it as part of  your marketing message as part of your  core beliefs and you hire people around  you know who want to help charities as  well but make sure that you have enough  at the end of the day to keep that  business going and pay everybody and  then as you start to build your business  you able to give a lot more back to  charity so people will work with you and  will bark from you because of the  charity aspect they might go you know a  little bit further because you work with  charity they might support a little bit  higher price because you work with  charity but it's not overwhelming you  still have to have a business model as  you know run a really good business have  great coffee have  service and I just want to make sure  that you have your systems in place so  that you're providing that quality  service and you're able to get past that  survival point so you can have a much  bigger impact when you are giving back  to to the charities that you believe in  so that's kind of number one to start  with if you you know don't have enough  money to get the company started what I  would try to do is partner up with the  local retail shop and just take over a  little part of their store and say can I  come in and you know sell my coffee and  you know baked goods on you know  whatever day of the week or maybe it's  everyday but just a small section of the  shop and you might have to pay a little  bit of that they might see it as value I  to their customers so they won't charge  you or they could take a percentage of  the profit that comes in but you don't  have to start the business with your own  location because that can be really  expensive and you'll make a lot of  mistakes so it's better to learn in the  low risk low cost way and as you start  to understand how to run this store then  you'll be better equipped to launch your  own store so I try to start with you  know within a local retail owner learn  the ins and outs try to learn from that  order to how they run their business and  you know dealing with staff and dealing  with just a retail operation start you  know small scale and then you can also  test the location so you know retail  location is huge you can figure out  pretty low risk if that location is  going to work for you or not and you  start to build your following and if it  is a good location and you're building a  following and you are certain to make  money then it's going to make sense to  go open up your own store and you'll  have the capital to be able to do it so  hopefully that helps I love to hear you  guys it to think if you want to leave a  comment under the video and if you like  the video please give it a thumbs up but  love seeing those come in so thank you  and we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

